{"seq":2,"slug":"pronunciation-and-intonation","title":"发音与语调","url":"/l-doc-books/h/english-learning/english-learning/listening-and-speaking/pronunciation-and-intonation","wordCount":1373,"readingTime":6,"html":"<h1 id=\"发音与语调\">发音与语调</h1><h2 id=\"概述\">概述</h2><p>发音（Pronunciation）和语调（Intonation）是英语口语的基础。发音准确让别人听懂你在说什么，语调恰当让别人理解你的意思和态度。对于中国学习者来说，英语中有许多中文不存在的音素和语调模式，需要有针对性地训练。</p>\n<h2 id=\"核心概念\">核心概念</h2><p>发音与语调共同决定口语的可理解度，二者解决不同问题：</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>发音（Pronunciation）</strong>：保证<strong>说清楚</strong>——音素是否发对，让听者能识别出你说的是哪个词。</li>\n<li><strong>语调（Intonation）</strong>：保证<strong>说明白</strong>——音高的升降传递意思和态度，同一句话用不同语调含义不同。</li>\n<li><strong>重音与连读</strong>：单词重音影响词义（REcord 名词 / reCORD 动词），连读与弱化是听力理解的常见难点。</li>\n</ul>\n<p>下图展示口语可理解度的构成：</p>\n<pre class=\"mermaid\" data-diagram-type=\"graph\" data-source=\"graph TD&#10;    S[&quot;口语表达&quot;] --&gt; P[&quot;发音 Pronunciation&quot;]&#10;    S --&gt; I[&quot;语调 Intonation&quot;]&#10;    P --&gt; P1[&quot;元音 / 辅音音素&quot;]&#10;    P --&gt; P2[&quot;单词重音 Stress&quot;]&#10;    P --&gt; P3[&quot;连读 Linking / 弱化 Weak Forms&quot;]&#10;    I --&gt; I1[&quot;降调:陈述 / 命令&quot;]&#10;    I --&gt; I2[&quot;升调:一般疑问 / 惊讶&quot;]&#10;    I --&gt; I3[&quot;升降 / 降升调:强调 / 言外之意&quot;]&#10;    P1 --&gt; C[&quot;清晰可理解&quot;]&#10;    I1 --&gt; C&#10;    I2 --&gt; C&#10;    I3 --&gt; C\">graph TD\n    S[\"口语表达\"] --&gt; P[\"发音 Pronunciation\"]\n    S --&gt; I[\"语调 Intonation\"]\n    P --&gt; P1[\"元音 / 辅音音素\"]\n    P --&gt; P2[\"单词重音 Stress\"]\n    P --&gt; P3[\"连读 Linking / 弱化 Weak Forms\"]\n    I --&gt; I1[\"降调:陈述 / 命令\"]\n    I --&gt; I2[\"升调:一般疑问 / 惊讶\"]\n    I --&gt; I3[\"升降 / 降升调:强调 / 言外之意\"]\n    P1 --&gt; C[\"清晰可理解\"]\n    I1 --&gt; C\n    I2 --&gt; C\n    I3 --&gt; C</pre><h2 id=\"英语音素系统\">英语音素系统</h2><h3 id=\"元音-vowels\">元音（Vowels）</h3><p>英语有约 20 个元音音素（因方言而异），远多于中文的 6 个基础元音。</p>\n<h4 id=\"短元音\">短元音</h4><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>音标</th>\n<th>示例</th>\n<th>中国学习者难点</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>/ɪ/</td>\n<td>sit, bit, fish</td>\n<td>容易与 /iː/ 混淆</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>/e/</td>\n<td>bed, red, head</td>\n<td>容易发成中文&quot;诶&quot;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>/æ/</td>\n<td>cat, bad, apple</td>\n<td>中文无此音，需张大嘴</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>/ʌ/</td>\n<td>cup, but, love</td>\n<td>容易与 /ɑː/ 混淆</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>/ɒ/</td>\n<td>hot, dog, stop</td>\n<td>英式英语特有</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>/ʊ/</td>\n<td>put, book, good</td>\n<td>容易与 /uː/ 混淆</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>/ə/</td>\n<td>about, teacher, the</td>\n<td>最常见的元音（弱读）</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h4 id=\"长元音\">长元音</h4><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>音标</th>\n<th>示例</th>\n<th>要点</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>/iː/</td>\n<td>see, eat, tree</td>\n<td>比 /ɪ/ 更长、更紧</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>/ɑː/</td>\n<td>car, far, heart</td>\n<td>张大嘴，舌位低</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>/ɔː/</td>\n<td>door, four, law</td>\n<td>嘴唇圆，舌位中高</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>/uː/</td>\n<td>food, moon, blue</td>\n<td>嘴唇圆，向前突</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>/ɜː/</td>\n<td>bird, her, turn</td>\n<td>中文无此音，需特别练习</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h4 id=\"双元音\">双元音</h4><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>音标</th>\n<th>示例</th>\n<th>发音要点</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>/eɪ/</td>\n<td>day, say, make</td>\n<td>从 /e/ 滑向 /ɪ/</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>/aɪ/</td>\n<td>my, time, like</td>\n<td>从 /a/ 滑向 /ɪ/</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>/ɔɪ/</td>\n<td>boy, toy, coin</td>\n<td>从 /ɔ/ 滑向 /ɪ/</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>/aʊ/</td>\n<td>now, how, about</td>\n<td>从 /a/ 滑向 /ʊ/</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>/əʊ/</td>\n<td>go, no, home</td>\n<td>从 /ə/ 滑向 /ʊ/</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>/ɪə/</td>\n<td>ear, near, here</td>\n<td>从 /ɪ/ 滑向 /ə/</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>/eə/</td>\n<td>air, care, there</td>\n<td>从 /e/ 滑向 /ə/</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>/ʊə/</td>\n<td>tour, sure, pure</td>\n<td>从 /ʊ/ 滑向 /ə/</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h3 id=\"辅音-consonants\">辅音（Consonants）</h3><h4 id=\"中国学习者的高频难点\">中国学习者的高频难点</h4><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>音素</th>\n<th>难点</th>\n<th>练习建议</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>/θ/ (th)</td>\n<td>think, three</td>\n<td>舌尖放在上下齿之间</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>/ð/ (th)</td>\n<td>this, that</td>\n<td>同上但声带振动</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>/v/</td>\n<td>very, voice</td>\n<td>上齿咬下唇（非 /w/）</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>/r/</td>\n<td>red, right</td>\n<td>舌尖卷起不接触任何部位</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>/l/</td>\n<td>light, feel</td>\n<td>舌尖抵上齿龈</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>/n/ vs /ŋ/</td>\n<td>sin vs sing</td>\n<td>/ŋ/ 舌根抵软腭</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h4 id=\"l-的两种发音\">/l/ 的两种发音</h4><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>位置</th>\n<th>名称</th>\n<th>发音</th>\n<th>示例</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>元音前</td>\n<td>清晰 l（Light L）</td>\n<td>舌尖抵上齿龈</td>\n<td>light, love, let</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>元音后</td>\n<td>模糊 l（Dark L）</td>\n<td>舌尖不完全接触</td>\n<td>feel, ball, milk</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h3 id=\"最小对立对练习-minimal-pairs\">最小对立对练习（Minimal Pairs）</h3><p>通过对比相似音素来训练辨音：</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>音素对</th>\n<th>词对</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>/ɪ/ vs /iː/</td>\n<td>ship / sheep, sit / seat, bit / beat</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>/e/ vs /æ/</td>\n<td>bed / bad, pen / pan, men / man</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>/l/ vs /r/</td>\n<td>light / right, lead / read, long / wrong</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>/b/ vs /v/</td>\n<td>berry / very, base / vase, boat / vote</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>/θ/ vs /s/</td>\n<td>think / sink, thick / sick, path / pass</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>/n/ vs /ŋ/</td>\n<td>sin / sing, thin / thing, ran / rang</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h2 id=\"重音-stress\">重音（Stress）</h2><h3 id=\"单词重音\">单词重音</h3><p>英语单词的重音位置会影响发音和词义：</p>\n<h4 id=\"重音规则-常见规律\">重音规则（常见规律）</h4><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>规则</th>\n<th>示例</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>双音节名词重音通常在第一音节</td>\n<td><strong>RE</strong>cord, <strong>PRE</strong>sent, <strong>OB</strong>ject</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>双音节动词重音通常在第二音节</td>\n<td>re<strong>CORD</strong>, pre<strong>SENT</strong>, ob<strong>JECT</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>以 -tion/-sion 结尾重音在倒数第二音节</td>\n<td>edu<strong>CA</strong>tion, de<strong>CI</strong>sion</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>以 -ic 结尾重音在倒数第二音节</td>\n<td>scien<strong>TI</strong>fic, rea<strong>LIS</strong>tic</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>以 -ity 结尾重音在倒数第三音节</td>\n<td>u<strong>NI</strong>versity, e<strong>LEC</strong>tricity</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h4 id=\"同形异义词-重音不同\">同形异义词（重音不同）</h4><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>名词</th>\n<th>动词</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><strong>RE</strong>cord（记录）</td>\n<td>re<strong>CORD</strong>（录制）</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>PRE</strong>sent（礼物）</td>\n<td>pre<strong>SENT</strong>（呈现）</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>PRO</strong>duce（产品）</td>\n<td>pro<strong>DUCE</strong>（生产）</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>CON</strong>tract（合同）</td>\n<td>con<strong>TRACT</strong>（收缩）</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h3 id=\"句子重音\">句子重音</h3><p>英语句子中，实词（名词、动词、形容词、副词）通常重读，虚词（冠词、介词、连词、代词）通常弱读。</p>\n<div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" data-lang=\"text\" data-code=\"重读词（大写）：&#10;I WANT to BUY a NEW BOOK at the STORE.&#10;&#10;弱读词（斜体）：&#10;I WANT *to* BUY *a* NEW BOOK *at the* STORE.\"><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>重读词（大写）：</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>I WANT to BUY a NEW BOOK at the STORE.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>弱读词（斜体）：</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>I WANT *to* BUY *a* NEW BOOK *at the* STORE.</span></span></code></pre></div><h2 id=\"语调-intonation\">语调（Intonation）</h2><h3 id=\"四种基本语调模式\">四种基本语调模式</h3><h4 id=\"1-降调-falling-tone\">1. 降调（Falling Tone）↘</h4><p>用于：陈述句、命令句、特殊疑问句</p>\n<div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" data-lang=\"text\" data-code=\"She is a teacher.          ↘&#10;Close the door.            ↘&#10;Where do you live?         ↘\"><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>She is a teacher.          ↘</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Close the door.            ↘</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Where do you live?         ↘</span></span></code></pre></div><h4 id=\"2-升调-rising-tone\">2. 升调（Rising Tone）↗</h4><p>用于：一般疑问句、表示惊讶/不确定</p>\n<div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" data-lang=\"text\" data-code=\"Do you like coffee?        ↗&#10;Really?                    ↗&#10;You are leaving?           ↗（表示惊讶）\"><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>Do you like coffee?        ↗</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Really?                    ↗</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>You are leaving?           ↗（表示惊讶）</span></span></code></pre></div><h4 id=\"3-升降调-rise-fall\">3. 升降调（Rise-Fall）↗↘</h4><p>用于：表示强调或感叹</p>\n<div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" data-lang=\"text\" data-code=\"That is amazing!           ↗↘&#10;I absolutely love it!      ↗↘\"><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>That is amazing!           ↗↘</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>I absolutely love it!      ↗↘</span></span></code></pre></div><h4 id=\"4-降升调-fall-rise\">4. 降升调（Fall-Rise）↘↗</h4><p>用于：表示犹豫、不确定或言外之意</p>\n<div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" data-lang=\"text\" data-code=\"Well...                    ↘↗（有保留意见）&#10;It is possible...          ↘↗（但不太确定）\"><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>Well...                    ↘↗（有保留意见）</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>It is possible...          ↘↗（但不太确定）</span></span></code></pre></div><h3 id=\"语调与含义\">语调与含义</h3><p>同一句话用不同语调表达不同含义：</p>\n<div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" data-lang=\"text\" data-code=\"&quot;You like it.&quot;（降调）→ 陈述事实&#10;&quot;You like it?&quot;（升调）→ 真的吗？（惊讶/确认）&#10;&quot;You LIKE it.&quot;（重音在 like）→ 你是喜欢的（强调&quot;喜欢&quot;）&#10;&quot;YOU like it.&quot;（重音在 you）→ 是你喜欢（不是别人）\"><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>\"You like it.\"（降调）→ 陈述事实</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"You like it?\"（升调）→ 真的吗？（惊讶/确认）</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"You LIKE it.\"（重音在 like）→ 你是喜欢的（强调\"喜欢\"）</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"YOU like it.\"（重音在 you）→ 是你喜欢（不是别人）</span></span></code></pre></div><h2 id=\"连读与弱化\">连读与弱化</h2><h3 id=\"连读-linking\">连读（Linking）</h3><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>类型</th>\n<th>规则</th>\n<th>示例</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>辅+元连读</td>\n<td>辅音结尾 + 元音开头</td>\n<td>an apple → /ə<strong>nˈæ</strong>pəl/</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>元+元加 /j/</td>\n<td>/iː/ 或 /ɪ/ 结尾 + 元音</td>\n<td>she is → /ʃiː<strong>j</strong>ɪz/</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>元+元加 /w/</td>\n<td>/uː/ 或 /ʊ/ 结尾 + 元音</td>\n<td>do it → /duː<strong>w</strong>ɪt/</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>加 /r/</td>\n<td>/ə/ 或 /ɔː/ 结尾 + 元音</td>\n<td>far away → /fɑː<strong>r</strong>əˈweɪ/</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h3 id=\"弱化-weak-forms\">弱化（Weak Forms）</h3><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>词</th>\n<th>强读</th>\n<th>弱读</th>\n<th>示例</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>and</td>\n<td>/ænd/</td>\n<td>/ən/ or /n/</td>\n<td>bread and butter</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>to</td>\n<td>/tuː/</td>\n<td>/tə/</td>\n<td>go to school</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>for</td>\n<td>/fɔː/</td>\n<td>/fə/</td>\n<td>wait for me</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>of</td>\n<td>/ɒv/</td>\n<td>/əv/</td>\n<td>cup of tea</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>can</td>\n<td>/kæn/</td>\n<td>/kən/</td>\n<td>I can do it</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>have</td>\n<td>/hæv/</td>\n<td>/əv/</td>\n<td>I have been</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h2 id=\"练习方法\">练习方法</h2><h3 id=\"1-跟读模仿-shadowing\">1. 跟读模仿（Shadowing）</h3><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" data-lang=\"text\" data-code=\"步骤：&#10;1. 选择 1-2 分钟的音频（带文本）&#10;2. 第一遍：只听，理解内容&#10;3. 第二遍：看文本跟读，模仿语调和节奏&#10;4. 第三遍：不看文本跟读（影子跟读）&#10;5. 录音对比，找出差距\"><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>步骤：</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>1. 选择 1-2 分钟的音频（带文本）</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>2. 第一遍：只听，理解内容</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>3. 第二遍：看文本跟读，模仿语调和节奏</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>4. 第三遍：不看文本跟读（影子跟读）</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>5. 录音对比，找出差距</span></span></code></pre></div><h3 id=\"2-录音自检\">2. 录音自检</h3><ul>\n<li>用手机录下自己的朗读</li>\n<li>与原音频对比</li>\n<li>关注：重音位置、语调走向、连读</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"3-每日发音练习-10-分钟\">3. 每日发音练习（10 分钟）</h3><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" data-lang=\"text\" data-code=\"5 分钟：最小对立对练习&#10;3 分钟：绕口令&#10;2 分钟：跟读模仿\"><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>5 分钟：最小对立对练习</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>3 分钟：绕口令</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>2 分钟：跟读模仿</span></span></code></pre></div><h3 id=\"经典绕口令\">经典绕口令</h3><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" data-lang=\"text\" data-code=\"She sells seashells by the seashore.（/ʃ/ vs /s/）&#10;Red lorry, yellow lorry.（/r/ vs /l/）&#10;The thirty-three thieves thought they thrilled the throne.（/θ/）&#10;Peter Piper picked a peck of pickled peppers.（/p/）\"><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>She sells seashells by the seashore.（/ʃ/ vs /s/）</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Red lorry, yellow lorry.（/r/ vs /l/）</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>The thirty-three thieves thought they thrilled the throne.（/θ/）</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Peter Piper picked a peck of pickled peppers.（/p/）</span></span></code></pre></div><h2 id=\"实践建议\">实践建议</h2><ul>\n<li>发音提升需要耳朵先行——先能听出差异，才能发出正确的音</li>\n<li>每天花 10 分钟做专项发音练习</li>\n<li>使用 Forvo.com 或 YouGlish.com 查听单词发音</li>\n<li>不要追求&quot;标准英音&quot;或&quot;标准美音&quot;，清晰可理解最重要</li>\n<li>找一个语言伙伴互相纠正发音</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"小结\">小结</h2><ul>\n<li>发音解决&quot;说清楚&quot;，语调解决&quot;说明白&quot;，二者共同决定口语的可理解度。</li>\n<li>中国学习者的高频难点音素包括 /θ/、/ð/、/v/、/r/ 和 /l/，可用最小对立对练习辨音。</li>\n<li>单词重音和句子重音会影响词义和强调重点，连读与弱化是听力理解的主要障碍。</li>\n<li>四种基本语调（降、升、升降、降升）传递不同含义，练习方法以跟读模仿和录音自检为主。</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"level":1,"text":"发音与语调","id":"发音与语调"},{"level":2,"text":"概述","id":"概述"},{"level":2,"text":"核心概念","id":"核心概念"},{"level":2,"text":"英语音素系统","id":"英语音素系统"},{"level":3,"text":"元音（Vowels）","id":"元音-vowels"},{"level":4,"text":"短元音","id":"短元音"},{"level":4,"text":"长元音","id":"长元音"},{"level":4,"text":"双元音","id":"双元音"},{"level":3,"text":"辅音（Consonants）","id":"辅音-consonants"},{"level":4,"text":"中国学习者的高频难点","id":"中国学习者的高频难点"},{"level":4,"text":"/l/ 的两种发音","id":"l-的两种发音"},{"level":3,"text":"最小对立对练习（Minimal Pairs）","id":"最小对立对练习-minimal-pairs"},{"level":2,"text":"重音（Stress）","id":"重音-stress"},{"level":3,"text":"单词重音","id":"单词重音"},{"level":4,"text":"重音规则（常见规律）","id":"重音规则-常见规律"},{"level":4,"text":"同形异义词（重音不同）","id":"同形异义词-重音不同"},{"level":3,"text":"句子重音","id":"句子重音"},{"level":2,"text":"语调（Intonation）","id":"语调-intonation"},{"level":3,"text":"四种基本语调模式","id":"四种基本语调模式"},{"level":4,"text":"1. 降调（Falling Tone）↘","id":"1-降调-falling-tone"},{"level":4,"text":"2. 升调（Rising Tone）↗","id":"2-升调-rising-tone"},{"level":4,"text":"3. 升降调（Rise-Fall）↗↘","id":"3-升降调-rise-fall"},{"level":4,"text":"4. 降升调（Fall-Rise）↘↗","id":"4-降升调-fall-rise"},{"level":3,"text":"语调与含义","id":"语调与含义"},{"level":2,"text":"连读与弱化","id":"连读与弱化"},{"level":3,"text":"连读（Linking）","id":"连读-linking"},{"level":3,"text":"弱化（Weak Forms）","id":"弱化-weak-forms"},{"level":2,"text":"练习方法","id":"练习方法"},{"level":3,"text":"1. 跟读模仿（Shadowing）","id":"1-跟读模仿-shadowing"},{"level":3,"text":"2. 录音自检","id":"2-录音自检"},{"level":3,"text":"3. 每日发音练习（10 分钟）","id":"3-每日发音练习-10-分钟"},{"level":3,"text":"经典绕口令","id":"经典绕口令"},{"level":2,"text":"实践建议","id":"实践建议"},{"level":2,"text":"小结","id":"小结"}],"prev":{"title":"听力策略与笔记","url":"/l-doc-books/h/english-learning/english-learning/listening-and-speaking/listening-strategies"},"next":{"title":"日常会话与表达","url":"/l-doc-books/h/english-learning/english-learning/listening-and-speaking/daily-conversation"}}